1.Django vs FastAPI
Django → Complete full-stack framework (admin, auth, ORM, etc.)
FastAPI → Lightweight, modern, high-performance framework focused on APIs

2.When to Choose
FastAPI → High-speed APIs, microservices, async needs, ML backends
Django → Full websites, rapid development, built-in admin & authentication

3.ORM
Object-Relational Mapper → Lets you work with the database using Python code instead of raw SQL

4.Full-Stack Big Picture
Frontend (React/Next.js)
↓ API calls
Backend (Express or FastAPI/Django)
↓
Database (MongoDB or PostgreSQL)

5.Key Security Habit
Always validate and sanitize every user input on the backend.

